{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbc-8d1e-7161-b034-85e889114404"},"sequence":60,"recorded_at":1780531400000115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b0649d13-c918-4732-aec0-765824cc6bc5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b0649d13-c918-4732-aec0-765824cc6bc5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b0649d13-c918-4732-aec0-765824cc6bc5"},"call_id":"call_01a0adbcacd77149a1128557dc3347b9","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2f5393/TASK-260830-2f5393_reviewer-cr1.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 1 of TASK-260830-2f5393 (implement-lease-record-validation-and-cas, first leaf of STORY-260830-1oqfec ownership-leases-and-fencing; siblings 3g12yp provider/pane fencing gates and 2atgj4 ownership reducer property tests follow; task_delta on the Story branch forked from trunk 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e (tip 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e), published by RUN-260917-98ac35 on muse-spark max, 12 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-2f5393_change-request_rev1.patch / _rev1-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-2f5393_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-2f5393_results.md, TASK-260830-2f5393_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-2f5393_producer-evidence.tar.gz (race/cover logs, mutants-03 per-plant raw logs, control-after.log), internal/sessrepo/TRACEABILITY.md in the candidate, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md (sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10; the task's scope text still cites v0.5.0 numbering — judge against the pinned headings and say where they differ).\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments, never the producer's alone: (1) Spec fidelity — quote the pinned Section 5.3 and 13.6-13.10 text on lease creation, renewal, expiry, epoch monotonicity, holder identity and compare-and-swap and diff each clause against lease_store.go; the producer decided that expiry is grant-expiry only (\"no time-expiring ownership lease\") and refuses fencing_grant_expired, never lease_expired — confirm from the pinned text whether the spec names an expired-lease refusal class anywhere in those sections or in the Structured error taxonomy; if it does, the omission is a P1 spec deviation, if it does not, record the clause that establishes grant-only expiry; confirm the canonical Lease Record identity stays with canonicaljson, the winning-lease admission of sessquery.winningLeaseFor is unchanged (diff the function against trunk 62d4463), and that sessrepo.CompareLeaseTuple restated across the import cycle agrees with sessstate.Compare — attack the agreement test by planting a divergence on one side (ordering of equal-epoch tuples, holder tie-break, an empty holder) and confirm it goes RED; state which tuple domain the agreement test enumerates (exhaustive alphabet or examples). (2) CAS and epochs — plant your own sequences through CreateLease/CompareAndSwapLease: epoch equal to the current, epoch +2, a CAS against a basis that is not the head, two CAS from different holders racing on the same basis (exactly one wins, loser gets the conflict class), a replay of a committed CAS (same bytes returned, no new blob — assert the blob directory is unchanged), a replay after the head moved (refused), holder identity with the same host and a different process, the same pid after a process restart (does the holder binding carry more than host+pid — start time, boot id, or an explicit holder token?), a fencing token minted for an older epoch presented after a newer lease, a token for the right epoch with a tampered byte. (3) Durability — lease blobs are immutable content-addressed files installed stage-then-rename with no index: how is the current lease found and what happens with two blobs for the same epoch from different holders (split brain) — probe it; rerun the injector-crash and real-SIGKILL suites twice; use AfterLeaseStage with your own fault injection to leave a staged-but-unrenamed file, a renamed file before directory fsync (simulate by crashing after rename), and a tampered blob — restart recovery must refuse or ignore each, never admit it. (4) Refusal census — enumerate every refuse site of lease_store.go (the producer claims 7 new sentinels and 26 narrowing plants, one per refuse site); each needs a named test reaching it through the production entry with the exact class; attack the census markers in census_test.go (7 new boundary markers, 3 equality ledger rows): remove one marker, move a refuse site, swap two adjacent arms sharing a class — the suite must go RED for each; report n-of-m with call sites. (5) Mutation — rerun testdata/mutate.py in an isolated copy against the exact final source (sha256 of lease_store.go must equal bdb89cb607268d1d06ac2eb235f4e1a22017d3da61899203be26d15153cac6c8), rerun each KILLED twice for determinism, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (epoch compare `>` to `>=`, holder compare on host only, token verification by prefix, expiry check off by one at the boundary) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators (NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL are unmeasured, not passes). (6) Bounds and docs — the provhost 5-site attestation bound holds (census the module for AttestLeaseRecord call sites), mint failures are operational errors not refusals (confirm a weakened grammar gate fails closed at mint), the ownership registry internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json still binds section:5.3 with the gap \"lease acquisition, renewal, expiry and fencing are not implemented\": precedent Stories (3drr2m, 3jqsx1, 3m2mw8, 2jylym) updated the registry and re-pinned reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 inside the implementing Story — grade the stale row P2 if any candidate document claims Section 5.3 lifecycle is implemented while the registry says it is not, otherwise P3 with the explicit requirement that a later leaf of this Story carries the registry update and digest re-pin before story_final; README/doc.go/LOGBOOK make no CLI or capability claim. (7) Hygiene — changed_paths are exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree; go test ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessstate ./internal/provhost -count=1 and -race green; go vet clean.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-2f5393/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-2f5393_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-2f5393_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-2f5393, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-2f5393_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
